; xfail: wrong number of arguments for Two: got 4, expected 2
;
; The same defect one grade further (2026-08-18): TWO arguments too many read
; far enough past the last field that the invented Type* fell outside mapped
; memory, and the COMPILER died with SIGBUS (rc 138) without a word — no file,
; no line, nothing to grep. Same fix, same message; kept as its own test
; because a crash and a wrong answer are different failures and only one of
; them could ever be noticed.

define Two (a: int  b: int)

let x Two(1, 2, 3, 4)
print("compiled\n")
